{
 "translation": "My head was spinning. I wished that Hitler would come and with his fiery people, tear open the heart of this wretched earth, in which the existence of impure humans would be incinerated. It was as if the whole world had set out to provoke me. Any sapling I plant, is it possible that the merciless claws of chickens would not scratch it? Any flower I pick, why wouldn't it appeal to my dead friends, and why wouldn't they make it the adornment of their hair buns? In short, the world has become hostile to my every word and deed. And how small is my world! Just these few lost souls, two or four second-hand lovers, and some crude, quarrelsome, and fashion-obsessed friends. Is this even a world? A completely exhausted world, how much lower and farther it is from my imagination! And now, it seems, even more dust has started to fly in this world. I feel like I was born before my time.",
